# DeployGuard configuration. The Go server reads real environment variables
# only (it does not parse this file), so load it with:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a; go run ./cmd/deployguard
#
# LOCAL MODE (default): needs nothing below. Keep every GITHUB line commented
# out: setting ANY GitHub variable switches to GitHub mode, which then requires
# the complete GitHub configuration.

# Loopback IP:port only in local mode. Default 127.0.0.1:8080 (":8080" in GitHub mode).
DEPLOYGUARD_LISTEN_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:8080

# ---- Optional AI summary (off unless PROVIDER or BASE_URL is set; then KEY and MODEL are required) ----
# Provider: anthropic (default) | openai | gemini | mistral. Each has a default public address.
# DEPLOYGUARD_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# Optional: a gateway or compatible server (no /v1 suffix). HTTPS, or HTTP on loopback only.
# DEPLOYGUARD_AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:20128
# DEPLOYGUARD_AI_API_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_API_KEY
# DEPLOYGUARD_AI_MODEL=REPLACE_WITH_MODEL_NAME

# ---- GitHub mode: all six REQUIRED together ----
# Positive integer, from the GitHub App settings page.
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_APP_ID=REPLACE_WITH_NUMERIC_APP_ID
# RSA private key PEM (multi-line). Easiest from a shell instead of this file:
#   export DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM="$(cat /path/to/app-private-key.pem)"
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=REPLACE_WITH_PEM_KEY
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=REPLACE_WITH_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
# Must exactly match the callback URL registered on the GitHub App.
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=https://deployguard.example.com/auth/github/callback
# HTTPS origin only: scheme + host, no path, query or userinfo.
# DEPLOYGUARD_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://deployguard.example.com

# ---- GitHub mode: webhook + Check Runs (optional; needs the plan workflow settings below) ----
# Secret configured on the GitHub App webhook. At least 20 random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Serves POST /webhooks/github and publishes the "DeployGuard" Check Run.
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_SECRET

# ---- Local-mode upload history (verdicts only, never plans). Default: history.jsonl in the user config folder ----
# DEPLOYGUARD_HISTORY_FILE=/absolute/path/history.jsonl   # or: off

# ---- Optional verdict history (GitHub mode; needs a role without superuser or BYPASSRLS) ----
# DEPLOYGUARD_DATABASE_URL=postgres://deployguard:REPLACE_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/deployguard
# DEPLOYGUARD_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# ---- Optional PR comment (needs the App permission Pull requests: write) ----
# DEPLOYGUARD_PR_COMMENTS=true

# ---- Optional plan provenance (GitHub mode; needs the App permission Attestations: read) ----
# File made by: gh attestation trusted-root > trusted_root.jsonl
# DEPLOYGUARD_PROVENANCE_TRUSTED_ROOT=/path/to/trusted_root.jsonl

# ---- Docker Compose database passwords (compose only; URL-safe characters, e.g. openssl rand -hex 16) ----
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_HEX
# DEPLOYGUARD_DB_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_HEX

# ---- Logging (all modes) ----
# debug | info | warn | error. Default info. Output is JSON on stderr; secrets are redacted.
# DEPLOYGUARD_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---- GitHub mode: optional ----
# Go duration between 5m and 24h. Default 30m.
# DEPLOYGUARD_SESSION_TTL=30m
# HTTPS URLs (GitHub Enterprise). Defaults: https://api.github.com, https://github.com
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_API_BASE_URL=https://api.github.com
# DEPLOYGUARD_GITHUB_WEB_BASE_URL=https://github.com
# Actions artifact retrieval: set BOTH or neither. Plain names, no / \ ? # or "..".
# DEPLOYGUARD_PLAN_WORKFLOW_FILENAME=deployguard-plan.yml
# DEPLOYGUARD_PLAN_ARTIFACT_NAME=deployguard-plan
# Basename only. Default tfplan.json.
# DEPLOYGUARD_PLAN_JSON_FILENAME=tfplan.json
# Header your own reverse proxy sets with the client IP. Leave unset otherwise.
# DEPLOYGUARD_TRUSTED_PROXY_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For
